  "provenance": "Stations read from a screenshot of the operator's site-status map in raymand.net's SHAMIM guide (figure 2, uploaded 2022-02; data/external_ir_shamim.refmap.jpg). The casters and the portal time out from outside Iran and Hoda Pro's station API needs a login, so this is the only position source reachable. Dots are map positions at about 4 km per pixel, georeferenced on the Natural Earth coast. They land a median 4.5 km from Natural Earth town positions, and agree to a median 3.3 km with the operator's own 2017 map once that map's constant 7.2 km pin offset is removed: town-level, not pillar-level. The 175 dots equal the 175 the same page declares. Names are a north-to-south index, not operator codes. Regenerated by scripts/regen_external_ir_shamim.py, whose docstring carries the measurement.",
